#
# Curated proper-noun allow-list for the production English system lexicon.
# One surface form per line; lines starting with '#' are comments.
# The lookup key is the ASCII case-folded form; the surface form here is the
# shipped canonical display. A curated entry always ships canonically: on a
# collision it replaces the folded SCOWL display at tier 9, regardless of
# which letters are capitalized (Apple, GitHub, PDF alike). Nothing is lost:
# the English Core emits the lowercase literal as a parallel arc (D071), and
# user-typed capitalization is authoritative over the dictionary display.
# (Clarified 2026-10-12: the previous sentence of this header described a
# leading-capital non-override rule that was never implemented and never
# shipped; the shipped data and the generator's merge step are the record.)
# Maintainers add entries only after review; see data-licenses/english/AUDIT.md §6.
